🔥 1. What is a Thread?
✅ Answer:

A thread is the smallest unit of execution inside a process that allows parallel execution of tasks.

🔥 2. Process vs Thread?
✅ Answer:
Process	Thread
Heavyweight	Lightweight
Separate memory	Shared memory
Slow	Fast
🔥 3. Why use Runnable over Thread?
✅ Answer:
Java doesn’t support multiple inheritance
Runnable allows extending another class
Better design (separation of logic)

👉 Killer line:
“Runnable provides better flexibility and is preferred in real applications.”

🔥 4. What is Race Condition?
✅ Answer:

Race condition occurs when multiple threads access and modify shared data simultaneously, leading to inconsistent results.

🔥 5. What is Synchronization?
✅ Answer:

Synchronization is a mechanism to control access to shared resources so that only one thread can access it at a time.

🔥 6. What happens without synchronization?
✅ Answer:
Data inconsistency
Wrong results
Hard-to-debug issues
🔥 7. Why is count++ not safe?
✅ Deep Answer:

Because it is 3 steps:

Read value
Increment
Write back

👉 Multiple threads can overlap here → wrong result